The local-profile argument gives a stronger result for fixed piecewise flat and curved profiles: any flat interval with density strictly between 0 and 1 forces M ≥ c(p)X, uniformly in the rounding phase. Its resonant transform has a nonzero step profile, which cannot have an everywhere nonnegative Fourier transform. I’m checking the rational coefficients and writing out that obstruction. The first E68 audit found no set with both a small bulk fraction and a substantially improved R.
